#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1365 expect=noViolation domain=SUPPDM
#note "Was `invalid_case_asymmetry` (finding SD1365-F2), the discriminator for two case regimes inside one Check. O-7 (Fix #338, ruling M2-D25): SUPPQUAL.RDOMAIN is bound by the CDISC Library to codelist C66734 (SDTM Domain Abbreviation) and DM is its submission value, so the RDOMAIN compare is now exact like the QNAM one. Row 1: RDOMAIN lower-case 'dm' is not the submission value -> does NOT fire (the casing is CT2001's to report). Row 2: RDOMAIN exact but QNAM lower-case 'saffl' -> does NOT fire, as before. Both regimes are now case-sensitive; a scenario that fires on row 1 has re-introduced the fold. The exact-case firing shape is pinned by invalid-SUPPDM."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset SUPPDM label="Supplemental Qualifiers for DM"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | dm | 01-701-1015 |  |  | SAFFL | Safety Population Flag | Y
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 |  |  | saffl | Safety Population Flag | Y
